title: 'Gnomon on Windows: status after W5, the local model, W4 phase A and P02 (2026-10-22)'
summary: |-
  Gnomon runs from the repo on the founder's Windows laptop.
  - The kernel runs on an owner-only named pipe and shields itself.
  - Claude Code sessions run at Low integrity with PowerShell (3d642944).
  - A local model, Ollama qwen3.5-9b-16k, runs sandboxed with tool calls (523ed66f).
  - Routine approval cards are approved by click through a helper-held Software-KSP key (ef24276e).
  - Probe P02 proved Windows Hello presence with an AUTH_MANDATORY Passport-KSP P-256 key (21ac9617).
  - Everything is committed on feat/gnomon-windows and not pushed.
  Next: W4 phase B (a Hello presence key for the fresh classes), then W6 (desktop app), then W7-W9 (signing, npm package, clean-machine test).
