body: |-
  ## Done on Windows (feat/gnomon-windows, unpushed)
  - W0 CI legs, W1 P03 + P02, W2 Rust helper, W3 kernel on a named pipe.
  - W5 session sandbox: Low integrity, restricted token, per-session SID, PowerShell tool / Bash denied, labels + session-SID ACEs, release at session end. The transport child is confined (outbound network not denied yet: P10w). Two Aegis reviews folded in.
  - Local model: `gnomon dev local --model qwen3.5-9b-16k`; the probe reads Ollama ctx; the GUI renders gnomon-local replies as "local model".
  - W4 phase A: click approvals for CLICK_KINDS (permission/ask-user/plan); presence 'click'; a click-class key refuses presence kernel-side.

  ## Open
  - W4 phase B: Passport KSP presence key (separate keyId) for fresh/root classes; the prompt needs a foreground owner window.
  - W6 wrapper (Tauri/WebView2) to replace the stand-in launcher; release gating, so approvals come only from the wrapper.
  - W7 Trusted Signing (needs the founder's account), W8 npm package + shim, W9 clean-machine test.
  - P10w WFP loopback deny, AppContainer for link/mod, the Developer Mode symlink tests.

  ## Dev workflow on this machine
  - The kernel runs via a wrapper stand-in script (dev up --wrapper); the GUI is opened by launch URL in a browser.
  - The test repo is C:\Users\ascen\gnomon-trial; the dev home is ~/.gnomon-dev.
  - Stop the kernel before rebuilding the helper (the approvals helper holds the exe).
  - On Windows, Python edits rewrite files with CRLF; prefer the Edit tool.
